KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ implicit default constructor: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ implicit copy constructor: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ trivial copy constructor: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The exception specification of implicitly-declared and defaulted
constructors ([except.spec]/6) is not computed: the noexcept operator
takes them as non-throwing (cpp_typecheck_expr.cpp, ID_noexcept), so
assertions 1 and 2 fail.  As for destructors
(implicit_exception_specifications), the specification has to be derived
from the constructors invoked for the subobjects.
